            "correct_answer": "$2e^{t}u(-t) \\leftrightarrow \\frac{2}{1-j\\omega}$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Time reversal keeps the coefficient and flips the sign in the exponent and in the frequency variable. So $x(-t)$ is the anti-causal version of the signal, and the spectrum becomes $X(-j\\omega)$.",
